    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d449">

                <pb facs="0520" n="416" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg416"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.00 Revolutions/373: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at São Paulo</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cameron</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">São Paulo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-09-20T19:00:00-03:00">September 20,
                            1932—7 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 20—5:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Manager of the Emprez at [<hi rendition="#italic">Emprezas?</hi>] Electricas
                    telephoned from Campinas that city bombed again this afternoon for the fourth
                    time, one bomb dropping in the repair shops of the Emprez at [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Emprezas?</hi>] Electricas situated half a mile from the
                    railway station wounding one workman damaging property.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cameron</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
